<%# One card delivery for the dashboard's card grid and Your board.
    (See Session#broadcast_update_to_sessions_index, lib/card_delivery.js,
    session_grid_controller.js and board_v2_controller.js.)

    The grid broadcasts on ONE stream, `sessions_index_individual`, but every
    open page has its own filters. The server therefore cannot decide whether a
    card belongs on your screen, so it does not try. It ships this envelope: the
    session's filterable facts, plus the card already rendered, and the page
    decides — replace the card, take it away, insert it, or ignore it.

    The card travels inside a <template>. Its contents are inert and its ids are
    not in the document, so an envelope for a session the page filters out never
    puts a second `session_<id>` on the page. The page's controller
    (`session-grid` or `board-v2`) reads the envelope, acts on it, and removes it.

    The facts mirror the dashboard's filters one for one: status, scheduling
    class, board visibility and CarPlay fit can change under an open page, so they
    decide removal as well as insertion. Genesis and agent root never change after
    a session is created; they only decide whether a session the page has never
    rendered may be inserted. The agent root is resolved the way the dashboard's
    filter resolves it: the recorded key, else the catalog root matching the
    session's repository and subdirectory.

    `board-category-id` and `last-touched` are where Your board puts the card.
    `read-at` is when the row was read, so a delivery that arrives late cannot
    undo a newer one.

    Locals:
      agent_session - the session
      restore       - true for the Undo reply (SessionsController#unarchive):
                      the operator is putting back a card this page just took
                      away, so it may return to whichever page it left
      read_at       - when the session was read (default now)
      card          - false to send the facts alone, for a change that moves a
                      card without redrawing it %>
<div data-session-grid-target="delivery"
     data-board-v2-target="delivery"
     hidden
     data-session-id="<%= agent_session.id %>"
     data-status="<%= agent_session.status %>"
     data-scheduling-class="<%= agent_session.priority_class %>"
     data-on-board="<%= agent_session.board_visible? %>"
     data-backlogged="<%= agent_session.backlogged? %>"
     data-carplay-fit="<%= agent_session.carplay_fit_bucket %>"
     data-genesis="<%= agent_session.genesis %>"
     data-agent-root="<%= agent_session.agent_root_key %>"
     data-board-category-id="<%= agent_session.board_category_id %>"
     data-last-touched="<%= agent_session.last_user_activity_at.to_f %>"
     data-read-at="<%= (local_assigns.fetch(:read_at) { Time.current }.to_f * 1000).round(3) %>"
     data-restore="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:restore, false) %>">
  <% if local_assigns.fetch(:card, true) %>
    <template>
      <%= render "sessions/session_card_frame", agent_session: agent_session %>
    </template>
  <% end %>
</div>
